    3   /*                                                                    
    4      ADVENTURES                                                         
    5                                SECRET MESSAGE:   ~ ==@ ") $ @"¦ )#:     
    6      VERSION NUMBER RATIONALE:                                          
    7              VERSION 0  -  ORIGINAL VERSION (WHATEVER THAT WAS)         
    8              VERSION 1  -  COMMON FORTRAN VERSION                       
    9              VERSION 2  -  PL/1 VERSION AS DISTRIBUTED BY SHARE         
   10              VERSION 3  -  ENHANCED PL/1 VERSION (FROM VERSION 2)       
   11              VERSION 4  -  THIS ENHANCED PL/1 VERSION (FROM VERSION 3)  
   12                                                                         
   13              FACOM VERSION MAY HAVE TO BE ENLARGED TO HANDLE            
   14              INCREASED DATA BASE SIZE DUE TO FACOM EXTENDED ATTRIBUTE   
   15              BYTES.  "*PROCESS" CARD OPTIONS "OPT(3),NOAIM" SHOULD BE   
   16              USED.       GP@SECV, 4/82.                                 
   17              (EXTENDED ATTRIBUTES NO LONGER SUPPORTED FROM C83031.)     
   18                                                                         
   19      CURRENT LIMITS:                                                    
   20        11200 WORDS OF MESSAGE TEXT (LINES, LINSIZ).                     
   21          800 TRAVEL OPTIONS (TRAVEL, TRVSIZ).                           
   22          330 VOCABULARY WORDS (KTAB, ATAB, TABSIZ, ATABB).              
   23          150 LOCATIONS (LTEXT, STEXT, KEY, COND, ABB, ATLOC, LOCSIZ).   
   24          100 OBJECTS (PLAC, PLACE, FIXD, FIXED, LINK (TWICE), PTEXT,    
   25                      PROP).                                             
   26           50 "ACTION" VERBS (ACTSPK, VRBSIZ).                           
   27          230 RANDOM MESSAGES (RTEXT, RTXSIZ).                           
   28           12 DIFFERENT PLAYER CLASSIFICATIONS (CTEXT, CVAL, CLSMAX).    
   29           20 HINTS, LESS 3 (HINTLC, HINTED, HINTS, HNTSIZ).             
   30           55 MAGIC MESSAGES (MTEXT, MAGSIZ).                            
   31                                                                         
   32     THERE ARE ALSO LIMITS WHICH CANNOT BE EXCEEDED DUE TO THE           
   33     STRUCTURE OF THE DATABASE.  (E.G., THE VOCABULARY USES              
   34     N/1000 TO DETERMINE WORD TYPE, SO THERE CAN'T BE MORE               
   35     THAN 1000 WORDS.) THESE UPPER LIMITS ARE:                           
   36                                                                         
   37        49999 MESSAGE TEXT WORDS                                         
   38         1000 NON-SYNONYMOUS VOCABULARY WORDS                            
   39          300 LOCATIONS                                                  
   40          100 OBJECTS                                                    
   41                                                                         
   42     SUSPEND/RESTORE PROCESSING, IN-CORE HASHING AND ENCODED DATA        
   43     BASE, THE "RED RUBY", ALL MAGIC MESSAGE AND WIZARD PROCESSING, AND  
   44     THE CRUCIAL CLEAR SCREENS ADDED BY GP, 12/81.                       
   45     DYNALLOC CALLS AND "LIBERATOR" PROCESSING BY GP, 7/83.              
   46     WEEK-END ALL-HOURS FINALLY FIXED BY GP, 10/84.    Y2K - GP 8/00.    
   47   */                                                                    
   48                                                                         
   49  PROGRAM: PROCEDURE (INPARM)  OPTIONS (MAIN)  REORDER;                  
   50                                                                         
   51        DCL  OBJECT       FILE RECORD                                    
   52             ENVIRONMENT(F RECSIZE(80) CONSECUTIVE);                     
   53                                                                         
   54        DCL  SOURCE       FILE RECORD                                    
   55             ENVIRONMENT(F RECSIZE(80) CONSECUTIVE);                     
   56                                                                         
   57        DCL  STORAGE      FILE RECORD                                    
   58             ENVIRONMENT(F RECSIZE(4800) BLKSIZE(4800) CONSECUTIVE);     
