  647                                                                         
  648  /*                                                                     
  649     CLEAR OUT THE VARIOUS TEXT-POINTER ARRAYS.  ALL TEXT IS             
  650     STORED IN ARRAY LINES- EACH LINE IS PRECEDED BY A WORD              
  651     POINTING TO THE NEXT POINTER (I.E.  THE WORD FOLLOWING              
  652     THE END OF THE LINE).  THE POINTER IS NEGATIVE IF THIS IS           
  653     FIRST LINE OF A MESSAGE.  THE TEXT-POINTER ARRAYS CONTAIN           
  654     INDICES OF POINTER-WORDS IN LINES.  STEXT(N) IS SHORT               
  655     DESCRIPTION OF LOCATION N.  LTEXT(N) IS LONG DESCRIPTION.           
  656     PTEXT(N) POINTS TO MESSAGE FOR PROP(N)=0.  SUCCESSIVE               
  657     PROP MESSAGES ARE FOUND BY CHASING POINTERS.  RTEXT                 
  658     CONTAINS SECTION 6'S STUFF.  CTEXT(N) POINTS TO A                   
  659     PLAYER-CLASS MESSAGE.  MTEXT IS FOR SECTION 12.  WE ALSO            
  660     CLEAR COND.  SEE DESCRIPTION OF SECTION 9 FOR DETAILS.              
  661     (VARIABLES INITIALIZED IN DECLARATIONS).                            
  662   */                                                                    
  663                                                                         
