 2886  /*                                                                     
 2887     CAVE CLOSING AND SCORING                                            
 2888                                                                         
 2889                                                                         
 2890     THESE SECTIONS HANDLE THE CLOSING OF THE CAVE.  THE CAVE            
 2891     CLOSES "CLOCK1" TURNS AFTER THE LAST TREASURE HAS BEEN              
 2892     LOCATED (INCLUDING THE PIRATE'S CHEST, WHICH MAY OF                 
 2893     COURSE NEVER SHOW UP).  NOTE THAT THE TREASURES NEED NOT            
 2894     HAVE BEEN TAKEN YET, JUST LOCATED.  HENCE CLOCK1 MUST BE            
 2895     LARGE ENOUGH TO GET OUT OF THE CAVE (IT ONLY TICKS WHILE            
 2896     INSIDE THE CAVE).  WHEN IT HITS ZERO, WE BRANCH TO 10000            
 2897     TO START CLOSING THE CAVE, AND THEN SIT BACK AND WAIT FOR           
 2898     HIM TO TRY TO GET OUT.  IF HE DOESN'T WITHIN CLOCK2                 
 2899     TURNS, WE CLOSE THE CAVE- IF HE DOES TRY, WE ASSUME HE              
 2900     PANICS, AND GIVE HIM A FEW ADDITIONAL TURNS TO GET                  
Aug 31, 2026  16:33     /***              ADVENTURE  -  PL/1 VERSION 4.0                  ***/                          
1.4.1                                               Source Listing                                           Page 51    
 2901     FRANTIC BEFORE WE CLOSE.  WHEN CLOCK2 HITS ZERO, WE                 
 2902     BRANCH TO 11000 TO TRANSPORT HIM INTO THE FINAL PUZZLE.             
 2903     NOTE THAT THE PUZZLE DEPENDS UPON ALL SORTS OF RANDOM               
 2904     THINGS.  FOR INSTANCE, THERE MUST BE NO WATER OR OIL,               
 2905     SINCE THERE ARE BEANSTALKS WHICH WE DON'T WANT TO BE ABLE           
 2906     TO WATER, SINCE THE CODE CAN'T HANDLE IT.  ALSO, WE CAN             
 2907     HAVE NO KEYS, SINCE THERE IS A GRATE (HAVING MOVED THE              
 2908     FIXED OBJECT!) THERE SEPARATING HIM FROM ALL THE                    
 2909     TREASURES.  MOST OF THESE PROBLEMS ARISE FROM THE USE OF            
 2910     NEGATIVE PROP NUMBERS TO SUPPRESS THE OBJECT DESCRIPTIONS           
 2911     UNTIL HE'S ACTUALLY MOVED THE OBJECTS.                              
 2912                                                                         
 2913     WHEN THE FIRST WARNING COMES, WE LOCK THE GRATE, DESTROY            
 2914     THE BRIDGE, KILL ALL THE DWARFS (AND THE PIRATE), REMOVE            
 2915     THE TROLL AND BEAR (UNLESS DEAD), AND SET "CLOSNG" TO               
 2916     TRUE.  LEAVE THE DRAGON- TOO MUCH TROUBLE TO MOVE IT.               
 2917     FROM NOW UNTIL CLOCK2 RUNS OUT, HE CANNOT UNLOCK THE                
 2918     GRATE, MOVE TO ANY LOCATION OUTSIDE THE CAVE (LOC<9), OR            
 2919     CREATE THE BRIDGE.  NOR CAN HE BE RESURRECTED IF HE DIES.           
 2920     NOTE THAT THE SNAKE IS ALREADY GONE, SINCE HE GOT TO THE            
 2921     TREASURE ACCESSIBLE ONLY VIA THE HALL OF THE MT.  KING.             
 2922     ALSO, HE'S BEEN IN GIANT ROOM (TO GET EGGS), SO WE CAN              
 2923     REFER TO IT.  ALSO ALSO, HE'S GOTTEN THE PEARL, SO WE               
 2924     KNOW THE BIVALVE IS AN OYSTER.  *AND*, THE DWARFS MUST              
 2925     HAVE BEEN ACTIVATED, SINCE WE'VE FOUND CHEST.                       
 2926  */                                                                     
